{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"Profiling found two pointwise bottlenecks: the compiled SiLU gate consumed 6–8% of long-case time, and RoPE recomputed trigonometry per head for large batches. I replaced SiLU with a tuned Triton kernel that is bit-for-bit identical to the previous fused output, and switched large RoPE cases to a shared frequency table. These changes should save roughly 0.05–0.15 ms depending on shape."}}
