{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"The backend comparison confirms PyTorch is already using the only supported flash implementation. A more productive result came from the residual-normalization path: a single Triton pass reproduces the native RMSNorm output almost exactly (fewer than 0.001% differing elements locally) while cutting each add+norm pair from roughly 50–85 μs to 15–47 μs. I’m combining that with an exact custom two-weight concatenation copy for the fourth run."}}
